{"id":"3875bc0ca63a0d8ad7d15e43d18fefc9c9799c04","axis":"silent","repo":"microsoft/onnxruntime","sha":"3875bc0ca63a0d8ad7d15e43d18fefc9c9799c04","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/Model_Loading_Performance.md","lines":["@@ -148,3 +148,32 @@ Ort::Session session(env, ORT_TSTR(\"model.onnx\"), session_options);"," The CPU prepacking option only parallelizes CPU EP kernels. The CUDA provider option only changes how external"," initializers assigned to CUDA memory are staged and copied; CPU and other execution providers retain their existing"," loading paths. They can be enabled together for models partitioned between CPU and CUDA.","+","+## Zero-copy external initializer buffers (`session.use_external_initializer_file_buffers_directly`)","+","+When an application supplies external initializer weights from memory-mapped files (for example `.onnx.data` or `.gguf`","+weight files mapped via `mmap`) using `AddExternalInitializers` or `AddExternalInitializersFromFilesInMemory`,","+ONNX Runtime by default copies non-owning CPU tensor buffers into a newly allocated internal CPU buffer during","+`InferenceSession::Initialize()`.","+","+Setting `session.use_external_initializer_file_buffers_directly` to `\"1\"` instructs ONNX Runtime to borrow naturally","+aligned CPU buffers larger than 127 bytes on little-endian hosts instead of allocating and copying a duplicate CPU","+buffer. Other buffers are copied. Tensors passed to `AddExternalInitializers` must be contiguous, non-owning views of","+user-owned buffers and contain native-endian values; allocator-owned tensors are rejected.","+Files passed to `AddExternalInitializersFromFilesInMemory` contain serialized little-endian values.","+","+```cpp","+Ort::SessionOptions session_options;","+session_options.AddConfigEntry(\"session.use_external_initializer_file_buffers_directly\", \"1\");","+session_options.AddExternalInitializers(initializer_names, initializer_values);","+```","+","+Borrowing is opt-in because it changes the lifetime contract: the application must keep each borrowed CPU buffer","+unchanged and alive until all sessions using it have been released. With the default setting, non-owning buffers can","+be released after session creation.","+","+Device tensors passed to `AddExternalInitializers` are always copied to owned CPU staging memory using the registered","+execution provider's data-transfer implementation before graph optimization or shape inference. They are subsequently","+copied to the device selected by the execution plan. This option does not enable borrowing device buffers, so caller","+device buffers can be released after session creation regardless of the setting. Session creation fails if no suitable","+data-transfer implementation is registered."],"additions":29,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"include/onnxruntime/core/graph/graph.h","lines":["@@ -761,8 +761,11 @@ class Graph {  // NOLINT(clang-analyzer-optin.performance.Padding): preserve exi"," #if !defined(DISABLE_EXTERNAL_INITIALIZERS)","   /** This function takes externally provided data for initializers with external data","    *    and replaces graph initializers with its content.","+   *    Tensors must reside on CPU for optimizer and shape-inference reads.","    */","-  common::Status InjectExternalInitializedTensors(const InlinedHashMap<std::string, OrtValue>& external_initializers);","+  common::Status InjectExternalInitializedTensors(","+      const InlinedHashMap<std::string, OrtValue>& external_initializers,","+      bool use_buffers_directly = false);"," ","   /** This function takes externally provided files in memory for initializers with external","    *    data and replaces initializers in this graph with their content. Subgraphs are not processed."],"additions":4,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"include/onnxruntime/core/session/onnxruntime_c_api.h","lines":["@@ -4161,12 +4161,19 @@ struct OrtApi {","    * replace them with the provided tensors. The API verifies that the TensorProto being replaced","    * has an external data reference and has the same name, dimensions and data type as its replacement. The replacement","    * does not apply to initializers in subgraphs and will occur before any of the optimizations take place.","-   * The data will be copied into the graph","-   * since TensorProto can't refer to the user provided buffers.","-   *","-   * Once the model has been loaded, the OrtValue(s) added to SessionOptions instance will be removed","-   * from the internal SessionOptions copy to save memory, the user provided buffers can then be deallocated","-   * and the SessionOptions instance that refers to them can be destroyed.","+   * Only non-owning tensors backed by user-owned buffers are accepted; allocator-owned tensors are rejected.","+   * By default, CPU tensor buffers are copied during session creation. Device tensors are copied to owned CPU staging memory","+   * before graph optimization and shape inference, using a registered execution provider's data-transfer implementation.","+   * Session creation fails if no suitable data-transfer implementation is registered.","+   *","+   * Setting \"session.use_external_initializer_file_buffers_directly\" to \"1\" enables borrowing naturally aligned CPU","+   * buffers larger than 127 bytes on little-endian hosts. Borrowed buffers must remain unchanged and alive until all","+   * sessions using them are released. Other buffers are copied. This option does not enable borrowing device buffers.","+   * Tensors supplied by this API must be contiguous and contain native-endian values.","+   *","+   * After session creation completes, non-owning buffers that were copied can be deallocated. The supplied OrtValue(s)","+   * and SessionOptions instance can be destroyed even when buffers are borrowed; the underlying borrowed buffers must","+   * still satisfy the lifetime requirement above.","    *","    * \\param[in] options","    * \\param[in] initializer_names Array of null terminated UTF-8 encoded strings of the initializers names."],"additions":13,"deletions":6,"truncated":false},{"path":"include/onnxruntime/core/session/onnxruntime_session_options_config_keys.h","lines":["@@ -423,10 +423,14 @@ static const char* const kOrtSessionOptionsOptimizedModelExternalInitializersMin"," static const char* const kOrtSessionOptionsModelExternalInitializersFileFolderPath =","     \"session.model_external_initializers_file_folder_path\";"," ","-// Use buffers supplied through AddExternalInitializersFromFilesInMemory directly for eligible main-graph initializers.","-// The application must keep each buffer unchanged and alive until all sessions created from the options are released.","-// \"0\": Copy initializer data during session creation. [DEFAULT]","-// \"1\": Borrow naturally aligned, native-endian initializer slices and copy other slices.","+// Use CPU buffers supplied through AddExternalInitializers or AddExternalInitializersFromFilesInMemory directly for","+// eligible main-graph initializers.","+// \"0\": Copy caller-owned CPU buffers during session creation. [DEFAULT]","+// \"1\": Borrow naturally aligned CPU buffers larger than 127 bytes on little-endian hosts and copy other buffers.","+// The application must keep borrowed buffers unchanged and alive until all sessions using them are released.","+// AddExternalInitializers accepts only non-owning, contiguous tensors containing native-endian values;","+// files contain serialized little-endian values.","+// Device tensors are always copied to owned CPU staging memory before optimization and shape inference."," static const char* const kOrtSessionOptionsConfigUseExternalInitializerFileBuffersDirectly =","     \"session.use_external_initializer_file_buffers_directly\";"," "],"additions":8,"deletions":4,"truncated":false},{"path":"onnxruntime/contrib_ops/cpu/quantization/matmul_nbits_impl.cc","lines":["@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@"," #include <cassert>"," #include <cmath>"," #include <cstdint>","+#include <cstring>"," #include <type_traits>"," "," #include \"core/common/common.h\"","@@ -39,7 +40,8 @@ void Dequantize4BitsKernelReOrder(","     return;","   }","   T* output_i = output + out_y * out_cols + out_x;","-  uint32_t quant_value = *(reinterpret_cast<const uint32_t*>(quant_data + element_offset / 2));","+  uint32_t quant_value;","+  std::memcpy(&quant_value, quant_data + element_offset / 2, sizeof(quant_value));","   if constexpr (onnxruntime::endian::native == onnxruntime::endian::big) {","     const uint8_t* c = reinterpret_cast<const uint8_t*>(&quant_value);","     quant_value = static_cast<uint32_t>(c[0]) |"],"additions":3,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"onnxruntime/core/graph/graph.cc","lines":["@@ -4415,9 +4415,15 @@ common::Status Graph::ReplaceInitializedTensor(const ONNX_NAMESPACE::TensorProto"," }"," "," #if !defined(DISABLE_EXTERNAL_INITIALIZERS)","-Status Graph::InjectExternalInitializedTensors(const InlinedHashMap<std::string, OrtValue>& external_initializers) {","+Status Graph::InjectExternalInitializedTensors(const InlinedHashMap<std::string, OrtValue>& external_initializers,","+                                               bool use_buffers_directly) {","   for (const auto& [name, value] : external_initializers) {","     const auto& user_tensor = value.Get<Tensor>();","+    ORT_RETURN_IF_NOT(user_tensor.Location().device.Type() == OrtDevice::CPU,","+                      \"External initializer \", name, \" must be copied to CPU before graph injection.\");","+#ifdef ENABLE_STRIDED_TENSORS","+    ORT_RETURN_IF_NOT(user_tensor.IsContiguous(), \"External initializer \", name, \" must be contiguous.\");","+#endif"," ","     OrtValue ort_value;","     TensorProto tensor_proto;","@@ -4426,8 +4432,12 @@ Status Graph::InjectExternalInitializedTensors(const InlinedHashMap<std::string,","     // contains std::string objects (with internal pointers), not serializable content.","     if (!user_tensor.IsDataTypeString() &&","         user_tensor.SizeInBytes() > utils::kSmallTensorExternalDataThreshold) {","-      if (user_tensor.OwnsBuffer()) {","-        // If the user tensor has its own memory, we avoid copying","+      const size_t element_size = std::max<size_t>(user_tensor.DataType()->Size(), 1);","+      const bool is_naturally_aligned =","+          reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(user_tensor.DataRaw()) % element_size == 0;","+      if (user_tensor.OwnsBuffer() ||","+          (endian::native == endian::little && use_buffers_directly && is_naturally_aligned)) {","+        // Keep ownership when available; borrowing caller-owned storage requires explicit opt-in.","         tensor_proto = utils::TensorToTensorProto(user_tensor, name, use_tensor_buffer_true);","         ORT_ENFORCE(utils::HasExternalDataInMemory(tensor_proto), \"Expecting this tensor_proto to have a pointer\");","         ort_value = value;"],"additions":13,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"onnxruntime/core/session/inference_session.cc","lines":["@@ -2926,15 +2926,30 @@ common::Status InferenceSession::Initialize() {"," #endif"," "," #if !defined(DISABLE_EXTERNAL_INITIALIZERS) && !defined(ORT_MINIMAL_BUILD)","+    const bool use_buffers_directly = session_options_.config_options.GetConfigOrDefault(","+                                          kOrtSessionOptionsConfigUseExternalInitializerFileBuffersDirectly, \"0\") ==","+                                      \"1\";","     if (!session_options_.external_initializers.empty()) {","-      ORT_RETURN_IF_ERROR_SESSIONID_(graph.InjectExternalInitializedTensors(session_options_.external_initializers));","+      for (auto& [name, value] : session_options_.external_initializers) {","+        const auto& tensor = value.Get<Tensor>();","+        if (tensor.Location().device.Type() != OrtDevice::CPU) {","+#ifdef ENABLE_STRIDED_TENSORS","+          ORT_RETURN_IF_NOT(tensor.IsContiguous(), \"External initializer \", name, \" must be contiguous.\");","+#endif","+          ORT_RETURN_IF_NOT(!tensor.IsDataTypeString(),","+                            \"External initializer \", name, \" cannot be a device string tensor.\");","+          // Graph optimizers and shape inference require host-readable initializer data.","+          Tensor cpu_tensor(tensor.DataType(), tensor.Shape(), CPUAllocator::DefaultInstance());","+          ORT_RETURN_IF_ERROR_SESSIONID_(data_transfer_mgr_.CopyTensor(tensor, cpu_tensor));","+          Tensor::InitOrtValue(std::move(cpu_tensor), value);","+        }","+      }","+      ORT_RETURN_IF_ERROR_SESSIONID_(","+          graph.InjectExternalInitializedTensors(session_options_.external_initializers, use_buffers_directly));","       InlinedHashMap<std::string, OrtValue>{}.swap(session_options_.external_initializers);","     }"," ","     if (!session_options_.external_initializer_files_mmap.empty()) {","-      const bool use_buffers_directly = session_options_.config_options.GetConfigOrDefault(","-                                            kOrtSessionOptionsConfigUseExternalInitializerFileBuffersDirectly, \"0\") ==","-                                        \"1\";","       ORT_RETURN_IF_ERROR_SESSIONID_(","           graph.InjectExternalInitializersFromFilesInMemory(session_options_.external_initializer_files_mmap,","                                                             use_buffers_directly));"],"additions":19,"deletions":4,"truncated":false},{"path":"onnxruntime/test/contrib_ops/qmoe_spin_pool_test.cc","lines":["@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@"," "," #include <filesystem>"," #include <fstream>","+#include <set>"," #include <system_error>"," #endif"," ","@@ -48,28 +49,32 @@ int64_t SumWithPool(qmoe::SpinPool& pool, ptrdiff_t count) {"," "," #if defined(__linux__) && !defined(__ANDROID__)"," constexpr const char* kWorkerThreadName = \"qmoe-spin\";","+using ThreadIds = std::set<std::filesystem::path>;"," "," // Worker threads are only observable through /proc, so tests that need the real thread count are Linux-only.","-int CountThreadsNamed(const std::string& name) {","-  int count = 0;","+ThreadIds GetThreadIdsNamed(const std::string& name) {","+  ThreadIds ids;","   std::error_code ec;","   std::filesystem::directory_iterator end;","   for (std::filesystem::directory_iterator it(\"/proc/self/task\", ec); !ec && it != end; it.increment(ec)) {","     std::ifstream comm(it->path() / \"comm\");","     std::string value;","-    if (comm && std::getline(comm, value) && value == name) ++count;","+    if (comm && std::getline(comm, value) && value == name) ids.insert(it->path().filename());","   }","-  return count;","+  EXPECT_FALSE(ec) << \"Failed to enumerate /proc/self/task: \" << ec.message();","+  return ids;"," }"," ","-// Thread names are set by the thread itself and a joined thread can linger in /proc for a moment, so poll.","-bool WaitForThreadCount(const std::string& name, int expected) {","+// A joined thread can linger in /proc and disappear after the baseline is sampled. Ignore baseline IDs, not a count.","+bool WaitForThreadCount(const ThreadIds& baseline, size_t expected) {","   const auto deadline = std::chrono::steady_clock::now() + std::chrono::seconds(10);","-  while (CountThreadsNamed(name) != expected) {","+  for (;;) {","+    auto ids = GetThreadIdsNamed(kWorkerThreadName);","+    for (const auto& id : baseline) ids.erase(id);","+    if (ids.size() == expected) return true;","     if (std::chrono::steady_clock::now() > deadline) return false;","     std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(2));","   }","-  return true;"," }"," #endif"," ","@@ -161,37 +166,54 @@ TEST(QMoESpinPoolRegistryTest, NameCurrentThreadSetsTheCallingThreadName) {"," }"," "," TEST(QMoESpinPoolRegistryTest, ShutdownJoinsWorkerThreads) {","-  const int baseline = CountThreadsNamed(kWorkerThreadName);","+  const auto baseline = GetThreadIdsNamed(kWorkerThreadName);","   qmoe::SpinPoolRegistry registry;"," ","   // A pool with N participants owns N - 1 worker threads; the caller is the remaining participant.","   qmoe::SpinPool& pool = registry.GetOrCreate(5, MakePool);","-  ASSERT_TRUE(WaitForThreadCount(kWorkerThreadName, baseline + 4));","+  ASSERT_TRUE(WaitForThreadCount(baseline, 4));","   EXPECT_EQ(SumWithPool(pool, 1000), 999 * 1000 / 2);"," ","   registry.GetOrCreate(3, MakePool);","-  ASSERT_TRUE(WaitForThreadCount(kWorkerThreadName, baseline + 4 + 2));","+  ASSERT_TRUE(WaitForThreadCount(baseline, 4 + 2));"," ","   registry.Shutdown();","-  ASSERT_TRUE(WaitForThreadCount(kWorkerThreadName, baseline));","+  ASSERT_TRUE(WaitForThreadCount(baseline, 0));"," ","   // The threads come back with the pools.","   qmoe::SpinPool& rebuilt = registry.GetOrCreate(5, MakePool);","-  ASSERT_TRUE(WaitForThreadCount(kWorkerThreadName, baseline + 4));","+  ASSERT_TRUE(WaitForThreadCount(baseline, 4));","   EXPECT_EQ(SumWithPool(rebuilt, 1000), 999 * 1000 / 2);"," ","   registry.Shutdown();","-  ASSERT_TRUE(WaitForThreadCount(kWorkerThreadName, baseline));","+  ASSERT_TRUE(WaitForThreadCount(baseline, 0));","+}","+","+TEST(QMoESpinPoolRegistryTest, ExitedBaselineThreadsDoNotAffectWorkerCount) {","+  ThreadIds baseline;","+  std::thread previous_worker([&baseline] {","+    qmoe::NameCurrentThread(kWorkerThreadName);","+    baseline = GetThreadIdsNamed(kWorkerThreadName);","+  });","+  previous_worker.join();","+  ASSERT_FALSE(baseline.empty());","+","+  qmoe::SpinPoolRegistry registry;","+  auto& pool = registry.GetOrCreate(5, MakePool);","+  ASSERT_TRUE(WaitForThreadCount(baseline, 4));","+  EXPECT_EQ(SumWithPool(pool, 1000), 999 * 1000 / 2);","+  registry.Shutdown();","+  ASSERT_TRUE(WaitForThreadCount(baseline, 0));"," }"," "," TEST(QMoESpinPoolRegistryTest, DestroyingTheRegistryJoinsWorkerThreads) {","-  const int baseline = CountThreadsNamed(kWorkerThreadName);","+  const auto baseline = GetThreadIdsNamed(kWorkerThreadName);","   {","     qmoe::SpinPoolRegistry registry;","     registry.GetOrCreate(4, MakePool);","-    ASSERT_TRUE(WaitForThreadCount(kWorkerThreadName, baseline + 3));","+    ASSERT_TRUE(WaitForThreadCount(baseline, 3));","   }","-  ASSERT_TRUE(WaitForThreadCount(kWorkerThreadName, baseline));","+  ASSERT_TRUE(WaitForThreadCount(baseline, 0));"," }"," #endif"," "],"additions":39,"deletions":17,"truncated":false},{"path":"onnxruntime/test/framework/inference_session_test.cc","lines":["@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@"," #include <atomic>"," #include <cfloat>"," #include <chrono>","+#include <cstdint>"," #include <cstring>"," #include <filesystem>"," #include <functional>","@@ -19,6 +20,7 @@"," #include <set>"," #include <thread>"," #include <tuple>","+#include <utility>"," "," #include \"nlohmann/json.hpp\""," #include \"onnxruntime_cxx_api.h\"","@@ -30,6 +32,7 @@"," #include \"core/common/profiler.h\""," #include \"core/framework/compute_capability.h\""," #include \"core/framework/data_transfer_manager.h\"","+#include \"core/framework/endian_utils.h\""," #include \"core/framework/execution_provider.h\""," #include \"core/framework/kernel_registry.h\""," #include \"core/framework/kernel_pilot_moe_expert_state.h\"","@@ -5286,12 +5289,483 @@ TEST(InferenceSessionTests, CompileApiWritesAndReloadsExternalInitializersBuffer","     }","     run_and_verify(session);","   }","+","+  {","+    // Verify AddExternalInitializers (external_initializers map) honors","+    // kOrtSessionOptionsConfigUseExternalInitializerFileBuffersDirectly for non-owning OrtValues.","+    const OrtMemoryInfo cpu_mem_info(CPU, OrtAllocatorType::OrtDeviceAllocator);","+    InlinedHashMap<std::string, OrtValue> ext_inits;","+    std::array<const void*, 2> expected_ptrs{};","+    std::array<std::array<float, 64>, 2> native_data{};","+    for (int i = 0; i < 2; ++i) {","+      const auto& init_proto = model_proto.graph().initializer(i);","+      void* slice_ptr = static_cast<char*>(external_buffer) + external_infos[i]->GetOffset();","+      if constexpr (endian::native != endian::little) {","+        ASSERT_STATUS_OK(utils::ReadLittleEndian<float>(","+            gsl::make_span(static_cast<const unsigned char*>(slice_ptr), external_infos[i]->GetLength()),","+            gsl::make_span(native_data[i])));","+        slice_ptr = native_data[i].data();","+      }","+      expected_ptrs[i] = slice_ptr;","+      OrtValue ov;","+      Tensor::InitOrtValue(DataTypeImpl::GetType<float>(), TensorShape{64}, slice_ptr, cpu_mem_info, ov);","+      ext_inits.emplace(init_proto.name(), std::move(ov));","+    }","+","+    // Without direct-buffer config, non-owning external_initializers are copied.","+    {","+      SessionOptions copy_ext_options;","+      copy_ext_options.graph_optimization_level = TransformerLevel::Default;","+      copy_ext_options.external_initializers = ext_inits;","+      InferenceSessionWrapper session{copy_ext_options, GetEnvironment()};","+      ASSERT_STATUS_OK(session.Load(model_buffer, static_cast<int>(model_size)));","+      ASSERT_STATUS_OK(session.Initialize());","+      for (int i = 0; i < 2; ++i) {","+        int index;","+        ASSERT_STATUS_OK(session.GetSessionState().GetOrtValueNameIdxMap().GetIdx(","+            model_proto.graph().initializer(i).name(), index));","+        const auto* actual = session.GetSessionState().GetInitializedTensors().at(index).Get<Tensor>().DataRaw();","+        EXPECT_NE(actual, expected_ptrs[i]);","+      }","+      run_and_verify(session);","+    }","+","+    // With direct-buffer config enabled, naturally-aligned non-owning external_initializers are borrowed in place.","+    {","+      SessionOptions direct_ext_options;","+      direct_ext_options.graph_optimization_level = TransformerLevel::Default;","+      direct_ext_options.external_initializers = ext_inits;","+      ASSERT_STATUS_OK(direct_ext_options.config_options.AddConfigEntry(","+          kOrtSessionOptionsConfigUseExternalInitializerFileBuffersDirectly, \"1\"));","+      InferenceSessionWrapper session{direct_ext_options, GetEnvironment()};","+      ASSERT_STATUS_OK(session.Load(model_buffer, static_cast<int>(model_size)));","+      ASSERT_STATUS_OK(session.Initialize());","+      for (int i = 0; i < 2; ++i) {","+        int index;","+        ASSERT_STATUS_OK(session.GetSessionState().GetOrtValueNameIdxMap().GetIdx(","+            model_proto.graph().initializer(i).name(), index));","+        const auto* actual = session.GetSessionState().GetInitializedTensors().at(index).Get<Tensor>().DataRaw();","+        if constexpr (endian::native == endian::little) {","+          EXPECT_EQ(actual, expected_ptrs[i]);","+        } else {","+          EXPECT_NE(actual, expected_ptrs[i]);","+        }","+      }","+      run_and_verify(session);","+    }","+  }"," #endif"," ","   allocator.Free(external_buffer);","   allocator.Free(model_buffer);"," }"," ","+#if defined(USE_CUDA) && !defined(DISABLE_EXTERNAL_INITIALIZERS)","+TEST(InferenceSessionTests, ExternalDeviceInitializersCopyBeforeOptimization) {","+  auto cuda_ep = DefaultCudaExecutionProvider();","+  if (!cuda_ep) {","+    GTEST_SKIP() << \"CUDA execution provider is not available\";","+  }","+  InferenceSession allocator_session{SessionOptions{}, GetEnvironment()};","+  ASSERT_STATUS_OK(allocator_session.RegisterExecutionProvider(std::move(cuda_ep)));","+  ASSERT_STATUS_OK(allocator_session.Load(MODEL_URI));","+  ASSERT_STATUS_OK(allocator_session.Initialize());","+  const OrtMemoryInfo cuda_memory_info(","+      CUDA, OrtArenaAllocator,","+      OrtDevice(OrtDevice::GPU, OrtDevice::MemType::DEFAULT, OrtDevice::VendorIds::NVIDIA, 0));","+  const auto cuda_allocator = allocator_session.GetAllocator(cuda_memory_info);","+  ASSERT_NE(cuda_allocator, nullptr);","+  const OrtMemoryInfo cpu_memory_info(CPU, OrtDeviceAllocator);","+","+  for (const auto& bias_shape : {TensorShape{}, TensorShape{1, 1}, TensorShape{64, 1}}) {","+    const bool scalar_add = bias_shape.NumDimensions() == 0;","+    const int64_t channels = scalar_add ? 64 : bias_shape[0];","+    ModelProto model_proto;","+    model_proto.set_ir_version(ONNX_NAMESPACE::Version::IR_VERSION);","+    model_proto.add_opset_import()->set_version(13);","+    auto& graph = *model_proto.mutable_graph();","+    graph.set_name(\"external_device_bias\");","+    auto set_value_info = [](ValueInfoProto& value_info, const char* name, int64_t channel_count) {","+      value_info.set_name(name);","+      auto& type = *value_info.mutable_type()->mutable_tensor_type();","+      type.set_elem_type(TensorProto_DataType_FLOAT);","+      for (int64_t dim : {int64_t{1}, channel_count, int64_t{1}}) {","+        type.mutable_shape()->add_dim()->set_dim_value(dim);","+      }","+    };","+    set_value_info(*graph.add_input(), \"X\", scalar_add ? channels : 1);","+    set_value_info(*graph.add_output(), \"Y\", channels);","+    if (!scalar_add) {","+      auto& weights = *graph.add_initializer();","+      weights.set_name(\"W\");","+      weights.set_data_type(TensorProto_DataType_FLOAT);","+      for (int64_t dim : {channels, int64_t{1}, int64_t{1}}) {","+        weights.add_dims(dim);","+      }","+      for (int64_t i = 0; i < channels; ++i) {","+        weights.add_float_data(1.0f);","+      }","+      auto& conv = *graph.add_node();","+      conv.set_op_type(\"Conv\");","+      conv.add_input(\"X\");","+      conv.add_input(\"W\");","+      conv.add_output(\"C\");","+    }","+    auto& bias = *graph.add_initializer();","+    bias.set_name(\"B\");","+    bias.set_data_type(TensorProto_DataType_FLOAT);","+    for (int64_t dim : bias_shape.GetDims()) {","+      bias.add_dims(dim);","+    }","+    ExternalDataInfo::SetExternalLocationToProto(ORT_TSTR(\"unused.bin\"), 0, bias_shape.Size() * sizeof(float), bias);","+    auto& add = *graph.add_node();","+    add.set_op_type(\"Add\");","+    add.add_input(scalar_add ? \"X\" : \"C\");","+    add.add_input(\"B\");","+    add.add_output(\"Y\");","+    const std::string model_data = model_proto.SerializeAsString();","+","+    for (const char* direct : {\"0\", \"1\"}) {","+      for (auto level : {TransformerLevel::Default, TransformerLevel::Level1}) {","+        SCOPED_TRACE(channels);","+        SCOPED_TRACE(bias_shape.NumDimensions());","+        SCOPED_TRACE(direct);","+        SCOPED_TRACE(static_cast<int>(level));","+        std::vector<float> bias_data(static_cast<size_t>(bias_shape.Size()), 2.0f);","+        Tensor cpu_bias(DataTypeImpl::GetType<float>(), bias_shape,","+                        bias_data.data(), cpu_memory_info);","+        OrtValue device_storage;","+        Tensor::InitOrtValue(DataTypeImpl::GetType<float>(), cpu_bias.Shape(), cuda_allocator, device_storage);","+        ASSERT_STATUS_OK(allocator_session.GetDataTransferManager().CopyTensor(","+            cpu_bias, *device_storage.GetMutable<Tensor>()));","+        OrtValue device_view;","+        Tensor::InitOrtValue(DataTypeImpl::GetType<float>(), cpu_bias.Shape(),","+                             device_storage.GetMutable<Tensor>()->MutableDataRaw(), cuda_allocator->Info(), device_view);","+        SessionOptions options;","+        options.graph_optimization_level = level;","+        options.external_initializers.emplace(\"B\", device_view);","+        ASSERT_STATUS_OK(options.config_options.AddConfigEntry(","+            kOrtSessionOptionsConfigUseExternalInitializerFileBuffersDirectly, direct));","+        ASSERT_STATUS_OK(options.config_options.AddConfigEntry(kOrtSessionOptionsDisableCPUEPFallback, \"1\"));","+        InferenceSessionWrapper session{options, GetEnvironment()};","+        ASSERT_STATUS_OK(session.RegisterExecutionProvider(DefaultCudaExecutionProvider()));","+        ASSERT_STATUS_OK(session.Load(model_data.data(), static_cast<int>(model_data.size())));","+        ASSERT_STATUS_OK(session.Initialize());","+        if (level == TransformerLevel::Default) {","+          int index;","+          ASSERT_STATUS_OK(session.GetSessionState().GetOrtValueNameIdxMap().GetIdx(\"B\", index));","+          const auto& initializer = session.GetSessionState().GetInitializedTensors().at(index).Get<Tensor>();","+          EXPECT_EQ(initializer.Location().device, cuda_memory_info.device);","+          ASSERT_NE(initializer.DataRaw(), device_view.Get<Tensor>().DataRaw());","+        }","+        int add_count = 0;","+        int conv_count = 0;","+        for (const auto& node : session.GetGraph().Nodes()) {","+          if (node.OpType() == \"Add\") {","+            ++add_count;","+            EXPECT_EQ(node.GetExecutionProviderType(), kCudaExecutionProvider);","+          }","+          if (node.OpType() == \"Conv\") {","+            ++conv_count;","+            EXPECT_EQ(node.GetExecutionProviderType(), kCudaExecutionProvider);","+          }","+        }","+        EXPECT_EQ(conv_count, scalar_add ? 0 : 1);","+        EXPECT_EQ(add_count, !scalar_add && level == TransformerLevel::Level1 ? 0 : 1);","+","+        // The session must not depend on the caller's device allocation after initialization.","+        std::fill(bias_data.begin(), bias_data.end(), -100.0f);","+        ASSERT_STATUS_OK(allocator_session.GetDataTransferManager().CopyTensor(","+            cpu_bias, *device_storage.GetMutable<Tensor>()));","+        device_storage = OrtValue{};","+        std::vector<float> input_data(static_cast<size_t>(scalar_add ? channels : 1), 1.0f);","+        OrtValue input;","+        Tensor::InitOrtValue(DataTypeImpl::GetType<float>(), TensorShape{1, scalar_add ? channels : 1, 1},","+                             input_data.data(), cpu_memory_info, input);","+        std::vector<OrtValue> outputs;","+        const std::array<std::string, 1> output_names{\"Y\"};","+        ASSERT_STATUS_OK(session.Run(RunOptions{}, NameMLValMap{{\"X\", input}}, output_names, &outputs));","+        ASSERT_EQ(outputs.size(), 1u);","+        const auto& output = outputs[0].Get<Tensor>();","+        EXPECT_EQ(output.Shape(), (TensorShape{1, channels, 1}));","+        for (float value : output.DataAsSpan<float>()) {","+          EXPECT_EQ(value, 3.0f);","+        }","+      }","+    }","+  }","+}","+","+TES